{
  "quest.332E026494C8D8E6.quest_desc": [
    "Battery boxes stop being enough once a reactor comes online.",
    "",
    "Place &aBank Cells&r and &2Bank Ports&r face to face and they join into one bank. Each cell stores 80,000,000 FE, and each port moves up to 65,536 FE a tick in or out, so add ports for more connections. A bank can be up to 128 blocks.",
    "",
    "Sneak + Right-click a port to change its look. Ports set to Gauge on one flat face join into a single fill display for the whole bank.",
  ],
  "quest.31D4DBFBA0954F8F.quest_desc": [
    "Both of these mine for you. The &2Pump&r collects fluids and the &aQuarry&r mines blocks.",
    "",
    "Place the &2Pump&r and it extends a pipe downward until it reaches a fluid. It takes &cHV&r input and draws 24 FE a tick while working.",
    "",
    "The &aQuarry&r needs more setup. Place two &aLandmarks&r on opposite corners of the area you want mined, then place the Quarry. The next quests cover it in detail.",
  ],
  "quest.335830B3FAC66753.title": "&6The Basic Generator",
  "quest.5AFE625D21EF516A.title": "Premium Junk",
  "quest.3C941658C37D10C3.title": "&3Machine Upgrades",
  "quest.5AFE625D21EF516A.quest_desc": [
    "The &aReprocessor&r turns junk items into &2Scrap&r, which is one of the best fuel sources at this stage for the Basic Generator.",
    "",
    "You can also convert 9 &2Scraps&r into a &dScrap Box&r, which you can use to get random loot drops that may contain some very good items.",
  ],
  "quest.0D883858A359F241.quest_desc": [
    "A &aCharge Pad&r charges everything you are carrying while you stand on it, so you do not have to put tools into a battery box one at a time.",
    "",
    "It stores 32,000,000 FE and takes &6IV&r input, so it accepts up to 262,144 FE in a single push from any cable that can supply it.",
    "",
    "Place one by the door so your gear recharges on the way out. Single Use Batteries and Energy Crystals are the portable versions.",
  ],
  "quest.72B4C9E61D90B60C.title": "&dAdvanced Machine Blocks",
  "quest.38A82B602CB754A3.quest_desc": [
    "An &aLV Battery Box&r stores 320,000 FE. Its front sends power out and every other face takes power in, and the side configuration button (I/O) in its screen changes any face. Generators produce unevenly and machines draw steadily, so a battery box between them keeps the machines running.",
    "",
    "A box has the same limit as a machine of its tier. Push more than 1,024 FE into an LV box at once and it burns out.",
    "",
    "&aEnergy Rectifiers&r still show in JEI. In this pack every machine accepts and supplies FE directly, so you do not need them.",
  ],
  "quest.31534FA4E511F2A0.title": "&dCarbon Armor",
  "quest.6B9F93CF811916D2.quest_desc": [
    "The &aMachine Block&r is the empty shell inside every &2LV&r machine. Every machine belongs to a voltage tier, and the tier is a limit on how much FE it accepts in one push.",
    "",
    "- &2LV&r: 1,024 FE. Macerator, Powered Furnace, Compressor, Centrifuge, Roller, Extruder, Canning Machine, Ore Washer, Powered Crafting Table.",
    "- &3MV&r: 4,096 FE. Reprocessor, Alloy Smelter and every Advanced machine.",
    "- &cHV&r: 16,384 FE. Quarry, Pump and Teleporter.",
    "- &6IV&r: 262,144 FE. Charge Pad and Antimatter Constructor.",
    "",
    "Push more than the limit into a machine at once and it burns out. Right-click it with a &aFuse&r to repair it, then fix what was feeding it. A &aTransformer&r upgrade in the machine raises the limit one tier per upgrade.",
  ],
  "quest.27D8AA95DE4FBCF1.title": "&aHydroponics",
  "quest.7421E8176E1FBD30.title": "&aMacerator and Compressor",
  "quest.3F24E0EC9E6206D0.quest_desc": [
    "Every basic machine has an advanced version that is faster and processes more at once.",
    "",
    "&aAdvanced Macerator&r, &3Compressor&r, &2Centrifuge&r and &bPowered Furnace&r are the ones you will use most. They are what lets a processing line keep up with a quarry. Each draws 128 FE a tick and takes &3MV&r input, four times what the basic machines accept.",
    "",
    "The &aPowered Crafting Table&r is worth building for convenience.",
  ],
  "quest.45150AA057377B1E.title": "&dTeleporters",
  "quest.23E977CDE5E3FD20.quest_desc": [
    "A &aQuarry&r digs out an area and collects everything in it. After this you no longer need to mine ore by hand.",
    "",
    "Mark the area with &aLandmarks&r, supply &cHV&r power, and put storage underneath it that can hold the volume, because it produces more cobblestone than you expect.",
    "",
    "A &aQuarry Filter Upgrade&r makes it mine only the blocks you pick, or only ores, and leave everything else in place. Skipped blocks cost no power.",
    "",
    "Pair it with a Reprocessor and a Scrap Box to turn the junk into something useful.",
  ],
  "quest.27D8AA95DE4FBCF1.quest_desc": [
    "Crops grow without a field once you can give them water and power.",
    "",
    "Build a &aHydroponic Accelerator&r. Put a seed in the seed slot and dirt or moss in the soil slot, then pipe in water. It uses 64 FE a tick and 250 mB of water per growth cycle.",
    "",
    "The seed and soil are never used up, so one seed keeps it running for good, and moss grows crops 1.25 times as fast as dirt. It grows wheat, beetroot, carrots, potatoes, melons and pumpkins.",
  ],
  "quest.31D4DBFBA0954F8F.title": "Quarry \\&\\ Pump",
  "quest.6B0BAB2876B04561.quest_desc": [
    "Smelting raw ore straight into an ingot leaves a lot on the table.",
    "",
    "Build an &aOre Washer&r. The Macerator turns each raw ore into 2 &2Crushed Ore&r, and the washer turns 2 crushed ore and 1,000 mB of water into 3 &aWashed Ore&r. A &2Centrifuge&r then turns 3 washed ore into 5 &aRefined Concentrate&r. Smelt the concentrate and every raw ore becomes 5 ingots.",
    "",
    "The washer uses 32 FE a tick and takes 20 seconds per wash. Crushed and washed ore also smelt straight into ingots, for 2 or 3 per raw ore on a shorter line, and a block of raw ore goes into the Macerator whole for 18 crushed ore.",
  ],
  "quest.3E100619DA6BB444.title": "&cReactor Components",
  "quest.126EA0089208EB6D.title": "&aCables",
  "quest.6B0BAB2876B04561.title": "&bWashing Ore",
  "quest.06E0165E2CC70DC3.quest_desc": [
    "&eFTB Industrial Contraptions&r is an all-in-one tech mod with generators, ore doubling, an alloy smelter, a quarry, a nuclear reactor and powered armor.",
    "",
    "In this pack it runs on plain &bFE&r. Its generators send power out of every side, its machines accept power on every side, and any cable or conduit from any mod carries it between them.",
    "",
    "The task item is made in a furnace, and most early parts need it.",
  ],
  "quest.21B8123C16D4EBC4.quest_desc": [
    "Copying a tested layout into a live reactor by hand is where mistakes get made.",
    "",
    "Craft a &aReactor Blueprint&r. Test a design in the &aReactor Simulator&r, then press Write Blueprint with a blank blueprint in your inventory. Use the written blueprint on the reactor and the layout shows as ghost items.",
    "",
    "Pause the reactor, carry the components and press Build from Inventory to fill every matching empty slot. The blueprint is never used up, so you can hand it to a friend to share the design.",
  ],
  "quest.332E026494C8D8E6.title": "&6Battery Bank",
  "quest.1D9DD2015E4B8903.quest_desc": [
    "Overclockers make a machine faster. This upgrade makes it do more at once.",
    "",
    "Each &aParallel Processing Upgrade&r adds one more copy of the recipe to every cycle, up to four copies with three upgrades. It fits the Advanced machines, the Alloy Smelter and the Reprocessor.",
    "",
    "Every copy draws the machine's full power, so four copies use four times the FE a tick for the same energy per item. Running out of power partway through resets the cycle.",
  ],
  "quest.3CF45D25F937845E.title": "&aCanning",
  "quest.5299C4304F1F14C2.title": "Useful Machines",
  "quest.64A56FA61F1BFADC.title": "&3Exact Batches",
  "quest.2D548E1B43587294.quest_desc": [
    "An &3Alloy Smelter&r combines up to three metals or materials into one. It is the first &3MV&r machine you will build and it draws 384 FE a tick, more than a Basic Generator produces, so it needs a better power source or a battery box.",
    "",
    "The goal here is &dAdvanced Alloy&r for the advanced machine casings. Any alloy smelter in the pack that makes it completes this quest, so building this one is optional.",
  ],
  "quest.45150AA057377B1E.quest_desc": [
    "A &dTeleporter&r moves you, and anything else that steps on it, to another teleporter. It needs a &aLocation Card&r to know the destination.",
    "",
    "A trip costs 800 FE for anything within 16 blocks and rises to 80,000 FE at 1,200 blocks or more. It takes &cHV&r input, so put a battery box or energy cell next to it instead of running a long cable.",
  ],
  "quest.3C941658C37D10C3.quest_desc": [
    "Machines take up to four upgrades in total in their side slots. Sneak + Right-click a machine while holding upgrades to install them.",
    "",
    "- &aOverclocker&r: 1.45x speed for 1.6x power, per upgrade. Four of them make a machine about 4.4 times as fast for about 6.6 times the power.",
    "- &2Energy Storage&r: adds 320,000 FE of buffer each.",
    "- &aTransformer&r: raises the machine's input limit one tier per upgrade, and with four installed it accepts any amount. Use this when a cable keeps burning out an LV machine.",
    "- &2Ejector&r: pushes finished items into the adjacent block.",
    "",
    "&7&oOverclockers stack, and so does their power draw. That is the usual way a first machine burns out.&r",
  ],
  "quest.7421E8176E1FBD30.quest_desc": [
    "The &aMacerator&r grinds things down. Raw ore becomes 2 &2Crushed Ore&r for the refining line, an ingot gives one dust, cobblestone gives gravel and gravel gives sand.",
    "",
    "The &aCompressor&r squeezes materials into denser forms. The one you need first is the &aCarbon Plate&r that goes into the &3Alloy Smelter&r recipe. It does not press ingots into plates. The &2Roller&r does that.",
    "",
    "Both are LV machines that draw 16 FE a tick, so one Basic Generator can run up to twenty of them.",
  ],
  "quest.06E0165E2CC70DC3.title": "Welcome to &eIndustrial Contraptions",
  "quest.2D548E1B43587294.title": "&3The Alloy Smelter",
  "quest.0D883858A359F241.title": "&3Charge Pads",
  "quest.2F9FF5E1FFBB7D56.quest_desc": [
    "&6Quantum Armor&r absorbs damage the same way &dCarbon Armor&r does, from a 120,000,000 FE capacity instead of 8,000,000.",
    "",
    "Wearing the full set with a charged chestplate gives you flight. Hold jump to go up and sneak to go down. Flight costs 40 FE a tick.",
  ],
  "quest.126EA0089208EB6D.quest_desc": [
    "You do not need the mod's cables. Any FE conduit, pipe or cable in your base connects directly to these machines, and the mod's own cables connect to other mods' FE blocks too.",
    "",
    "If you use them anyway, check the rating. An &aLV Cable&r carries 1,024 FE a tick, and each tier carries four times the one below it. Send more than that through a cable and it becomes a &cBurnt Cable&r. Burnt cables cannot be repaired. Break it, turn it into &aScrap&r and place the right tier.",
    "",
    "A cable only joins cables of its own tier, so an LV line placed against an MV line does not connect to it. At the top end, the &dSuperconducting Cable&r has no transfer limit and never burns out.",
  ],
  "quest.335830B3FAC66753.quest_desc": [
    "Your first power source is the &aBasic Generator&r, which produces &b320 FE&r a tick. It only burns coal, charcoal, coal blocks, logs, planks, sticks, saplings, sugar cane, cactus and &aScrap&r. Other furnace fuels, such as lava buckets and blaze rods, do nothing in it.",
    "",
    "It sends power out of every side, so a machine placed against it runs with no cable. Anything further away needs an FE cable.",
    "",
    "Fuel that is already lit burns to the end even when the buffer is full. Connect it to something that uses or stores the power or that fuel is wasted.",
    "",
    "The &aGeothermal Generator&r, &2Wind Mill&r and solar panels are the passive options at this tier. The Power chapter covers them.",
  ],
  "task.4AC01432CCABFAA1.title": "Quarry",
  "quest.38A82B602CB754A3.title": "&3Battery Boxes",
  "quest.48AB0F2C91CA731D.quest_desc": [
    "The &6Nuclear Reactor&r produces tens of thousands of FE a tick when it is laid out well, and explodes when it is not. In this pack its output is four times the mod's default, so a small design produces a lot.",
    "",
    "There are three things to balance, &cHeat&r from the fuel rods, &3Cooling&r from vents and coolant cells, and the &bpower&r output. The reactor only explodes when stored heat reaches 100%.",
    "",
    "[\"\", \"Power leaves the reactor on every side as FE. The next quest covers the parts, and the mod's \", {\"text\": \"reactor guide\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"click_event\": {\"action\": \"custom\", \"id\": \"ftbquests:docs\", \"payload\": {\"location\": \"guideme,ftbic:guide,ftbic:nuclear/index.md\"}}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Open the Nuclear Reactor pages in the Industrial Contraptions guide\"}}, \" has the full tables.\"]",
  ],
  "quest.21B8123C16D4EBC4.title": "&cBlueprints",
  "quest.3F24E0EC9E6206D0.title": "&dAdvanced Machines",
  "quest.23E977CDE5E3FD20.title": "&6The Quarry",
  "quest.156F99299E2A30F9.quest_desc": [
    "Almost everything in this mod wants a circuit.",
    "",
    "&aElectronic Circuits&r come first. &2Advanced Circuits&r follow, and &aIridium Circuits&r sit at the top.",
    "",
    "Get a steady circuit supply going early. Every tier above this one is gated behind it.",
  ],
  "quest.6B9F93CF811916D2.title": "Machine Tiers",
  "quest.1D9DD2015E4B8903.title": "&dParallel Processing",
  "task.7E769A4ACA1F66B4.title": "Other Basic Generators",
  "quest.156F99299E2A30F9.title": "&aCircuits",
  "quest.48D3937A90BD8669.title": "&dFamily Trees",
  "quest.2BD6E508BB0CE73F.quest_desc": [
    "The &aAdvanced Hydroponic Accelerator&r has four lanes, each with its own seed and soil, so it grows four crops at once.",
    "",
    "Switch it to Mutation mode and lanes 1 and 2, and lanes 3 and 4, each cross two parents. A Carrot and a Potato can give Beetroot Seeds, and Wheat Seeds with Beetroot Seeds can give Melon Seeds, each at a 15% chance. A failed cross returns both parents.",
    "",
    "With &eProductive Farming&r traits on the parents, the one with the higher Mutability raises that chance, and the new seed takes its traits.",
  ],
  "quest.72B4C9E61D90B60C.quest_desc": [
    "&dAdvanced Machine Blocks&r are the base for every advanced machine from this point on. All of them take &3MV&r input, so plan the power supply to match.",
  ],
  "quest.5299C4304F1F14C2.quest_desc": [
    "A &2Centrifuge&r extracts extra items from some resources, such as dyes, silicon gems and gravel.",
    "",
    "The &aExtruder&r and the &2Roller&r turn metal ingots into plates and rods.",
  ],
  "quest.3E100619DA6BB444.quest_desc": [
    "An FTBIC reactor is a puzzle. Fuel rods make heat and power, and everything else in the chamber exists to stop the heat killing it.",
    "",
    "- &aHeat Vents&r shed heat, in component, reactor and overclocked flavors.",
    "- &aHeat Exchangers&r move heat between components so nothing runs away.",
    "- &aCoolant Cells&r in small, medium and large soak it up.",
    "- &aNeutron Reflectors&r bounce output back into the fuel for more power.",
    "",
    "&cBuild it wrong and it melts down.&r Use the &aReactor Simulator&r to test a layout before you put a single rod in.",
    "",
    "Reactor Plating raises the chamber's heat capacity if you need headroom.",
  ],
  "quest.48D3937A90BD8669.quest_desc": [
    "This pack gives &eMystical Agriculture&r a family tree of crosses, so the &aAdvanced Hydroponic Accelerator&r can breed new resource seeds.",
    "",
    "39 of its seeds can come out of Mutation mode as well as the Infusion Altar. A cross costs only the two parents, water and power, with no essence. It starts from the elemental seeds: Earth and Fire give Stone, Coal and Stone give Copper.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Basic crosses succeed 40 to 50% of the time, ores 20 to 30%, and Diamond, Emerald, Netherite, Iridium and Platinum 12%. A failed cross hands both parents back.",
    "",
    "&eProductive Farming&r Mutability on the stronger parent adds half the base chance per level, so Mutability 4 turns 12% into 36%. Grow parents in a normal lane first, since harvests raise their traits.",
    "",
    "[\"\", {\"text\": \"Crop Mutation\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"click_event\": {\"action\": \"custom\", \"id\": \"ftbquests:docs\", \"payload\": {\"location\": \"guideme,ftb:crop_mutation,ftb:index.md\"}}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Open the Crop Mutation guide\"}}, \" lays out the whole tree and every pair.\"]",
  ],
  "quest.64A56FA61F1BFADC.quest_desc": [
    "A recipe with two ingredients jams the moment a pipe fills both slots with the same one.",
    "",
    "Craft a &aBatch Feeder&r and a &2Configuration Card&r. Point the feeder's outlet at a machine and set up to three items and one fluid in its ghost slots, such as 3 copper and 1 tin for bronze. It only sends a complete batch, never part of one, and needs no power.",
    "",
    "Every machine has a side configuration button (I/O) that sets what each face takes in and gives out, and a lock button that ties an input slot to one item. Sneak + Right-click a machine with the Configuration Card to copy those settings, then right-click another machine of the same type to paste them.",
  ],
  "quest.7FB19A7D0A3292D6.quest_desc": [
    "&eIndustrial Contraptions&r is one of the few mods here where &avoltage&r still matters. Power runs at &aLV&r, &3MV&r, &cHV&r, &dEV&r and &6IV&r, and each tier has its own cables, transformers and battery boxes.",
    "",
    "&aTransformers&r are for networks built from the mod's own cables. Each one steps power down one tier. An &aLV Transformer&r takes 4,096 FE a tick in from the MV side and sends 1,024 out to LV.",
    "",
    "On an FE cable there is nothing to step down. The only number that matters is the machine's own limit, and the &aTransformer&r upgrade raises it.",
    "",
    "&7&oReinforced Cables carry the same rate as plain ones and can be used as part of a reactor wall.&r",
  ],
  "quest.2F9FF5E1FFBB7D56.title": "&6Quantum Armor",
  "quest.7FB19A7D0A3292D6.title": "&bVoltage Tiers",
  "quest.2BD6E508BB0CE73F.title": "&dCrossbreeding",
  "quest.16D8629C1CE0B2DE.quest_desc": [
    "One &dAntimatter&r costs 8,000,000 FE in the &6Antimatter Constructor&r. The constructor only accepts &6IV&r input, so it needs a large power source such as a reactor.",
    "",
    "Antimatter is used in the &6Quantum&r armor set and the other top-tier recipes.",
    "",
    "&aScrap&r and &2Scrap Boxes&r placed in the constructor speed it up.",
  ],
  "quest.48AB0F2C91CA731D.title": "&6Nuclear Power",
  "quest.31534FA4E511F2A0.quest_desc": [
    "&dCarbon Armor&r is the mid-tier set, and it is powered. Every point of damage it absorbs costs 40,000 FE from the chestplate's 8,000,000 FE capacity instead of durability, so keep it charged.",
    "",
    "The chestplate absorbs 35% of each hit, and a matching helmet, leggings and boots add 25%, 35% and 15%, so the full set blocks all of it. All of that power comes from the chestplate, and once it runs dry the other pieces stop absorbing too.",
    "",
    "It is the step before the &dQuantum&r set. The Mechanical Elytra is worth making at the same time.",
  ],
  "quest.3CF45D25F937845E.quest_desc": [
    "The &aCanning Machine&r seals food into &2Canned Food&r that never spoils and stacks well.",
    "",
    "It also makes Spray Paint Cans and &aUranium Fuel Rods&r, and each of those uses up a &2Fluid Cell&r of water. Fill an empty cell by right-clicking a water source with it.",
    "",
    "&7&oThe Feed The Beast™ Protein Bar is in here somewhere too.&r",
  ],
  "quest.16D8629C1CE0B2DE.title": "&dAntimatter",
}